<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH C.BANK SETS 13-WEEK BILL AUCTION AT 12.4 PCT.</title>
<headline>CZECH C.BANK SETS 13-WEEK BILL AUCTION AT 12.4 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech National Bank on Wednesday set a Dutch auction offering five billion crowns in 13-week central bank liquidity bills for Thursday.</p>
<p>In a statement, the central bank said the limit price on bids would imply a maximum gross yield of 12.4 percent and a net yield of 9.3 percent.</p>
<p>Gross yield in the last auction of similar bills was 12.75 percent on January 9.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
